\newlabel{fig:pesaran}{{1}{5}{The classical GVAR pipeline. Country models are estimated one at a time on their own samples, linked by weakly exogenous trade-weighted stars built from observed data, then stacked through the link matrices and inverted once to give the world reduced form \eqref {eq:stack}. The two red tags mark the assumptions the MFFM replaces: weak exogeneity and the common balanced estimation window}{figure.1}{}}
